Use a struct when a few values belong together. A game can keep each
player's name and score in one value.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    Player = |
        name String,
        score I32 = 0,
    |
]

The pipes enclose the fields. Each field declares a name and a type. The
score also has a default, so you can create a player with just a name.
Declaring another struct with these same fields creates a different type.
